{"name":"Papyrus Map","hex":"#c0ac92","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"papyrus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant (Cyperus papyrus) in the sedge family, native to the Nile river valley, paper reed.","A material similar to paper made from the papyrus plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/papyrus"},{"term":"map","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-5 language code for Austronesian languages."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A visual representation of an area, whether real or imaginary, showing the relative positions of places and other features.","A graphical or logical representation of any structure or system, showing the positions of or relationships between its components."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/map"}],"entries":[{"title":"Papyrus","blocks":[{"text":"Papyrus is a substance used in ancient times as a writing surface. Similar to thick paper, it was first known to have been used in Egypt as the papyrus plant from which it was created was once abundant across the Nile Delta. Papyrus was made from the pith of the papyrus plant, Cyperus papyrus, a wetland sedge. Papyrus can also refer to a document written on sheets of such material, joined side by side and rolled up into a scroll, an early form of a book."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Papyrus.jpg/330px-Papyrus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Papyrus","wikidata":"Q125576"},{"title":"Map","blocks":[{"text":"In cartography, a map is a representation or abstraction of geographic reality. Maps are used for a wide range of purposes, including navigation, scientific research, governance, and warfare. A common use is route planning, which enables users to find their way to their destination. Specialized maps called charts are used for nautical navigation and aviation. Scientists use maps to organize spatial data in fields such as geology, meteorology, seismology and demographics. Governments use maps for administrative functions such as census, electoral districts, property taxation, dispatching police, and coordinating disaster relief. Military and security organizations use maps for mission planning, surveillance, border management, logistics, and intelligence analysis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/World_Map_1689.JPG/330px-World_Map_1689.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Map","wikidata":"Q4006"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Letter_on_Papyrus.jpg/500px-Letter_on_Papyrus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Letter_on_Papyrus.jpg/500px-Letter_on_Papyrus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An official letter on a papyrus of the 3rd century BCE","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALetter_on_Papyrus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Busto_maschile.JPG/500px-Busto_maschile.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Busto_maschile.JPG/1280px-Busto_maschile.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Busto_maschile.JPG/500px-Busto_maschile.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Roman portraiture fresco of a young man with a papyrus scroll, from Herculaneum, 1st century CE","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABusto_maschile.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Book_of_the_Dead_of_Hunefer_sheet_3.jpg/500px-Book_of_the_Dead_of_H